==Icelandic==

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/ˈeiːɣa/|lang=is}}
*: {{rhymes|eiːɣa|lang=is}}

===Etymology 1===
From {{etyl|non|is}} {{m|non|eiga}}, from {{etyl|gem-pro|is}} {{m|gem-pro|*aiganą}}.

====Verb====
{{is-verb-preterite|á|átti|átt}}

# {{label|is|transitive|governs the accusative}} to [[have]], to be [[closely]] related to
#: ''Ég '''á''' skemmtilega konu.''
#:: I '''have''' a funny wife.
# {{label|is|transitive|governs the accusative}} to [[possess]], to [[own]]{{jump|possess|s}}
# to [[have to]], [[should]]{{jump|have to|s}}
#: ''Hann '''á''' að mæta í skólann, sama hvað foreldrar hans segja.''
#:: He's '''supposed''' to show up for school, regardless of what his parents say.
# to be [[said]] to be by others
#: ''The Matrix '''á''' að vera skemmtileg mynd.''
#:: '''They say''' The Matrix is a good movie.

